Description: Pimax Crystal Super / Dream Air / Crystal VR hub for Linux
 PiBridge is a one-app, one-click VR hub for Pimax headsets (Crystal Super,
 Dream Air and the original Crystal) on Linux: a Qt 6 desktop app plus the
 engine binaries for inside-out tracking, eye tracking, controller tracking,
 room setup, video recording, the in-headset overlay and a VR home.
 .
 VR runs on one of two backends: SteamVR (the headset shown through
 CustomHeadsetOpenVR, installed by the user) or Monado (PiBridge's Monado fork,
 package pibridge-monado, with PiBridge World as the home, shipped as one
 executable built with Godot's release template). OpenCV, the Vulkan loader, Qt 6, ffmpeg
 and every other library are used from their system packages.
 .
 The per-user setup (enabling the user services) is done by the app on first
 run. The optional Pimax-engine inside-out path needs winbridge, shipped as
 source and built with pibridge-build-winbridge (Suggests: wine, mingw-w64),
 and the Pimax kit, which is not shipped.

Package: pibridge-monado
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 pibridge (= ${binary:Version}),
 libcap2-bin,
Description: PiBridge's Monado fork: the Monado backend of PiBridge
 The OpenXR runtime of PiBridge's Monado backend: Monado 25.1 with the Pimax
 driver (Crystal Super, Dream Air, the original Crystal), the Lighthouse
 builder over Valve's driver_lighthouse from the user's SteamVR, PiBridge's
 recenter, eye gaze and recorder tap. Installed under
 /usr/lib/pibridge/monado, apart from any distribution Monado; the PiBridge app
 starts it and points the OpenXR runtime at it when Monado is the chosen
 backend. monado-service is given cap_sys_nice (realtime compositor threads)
 at install.
